abstract: >-
  ORCA Web Lab is a web-based computational chemistry platform designed for
  molecular structure exploration, ORCA input generation, quantum-chemistry
  calculations, result analysis, and fault-tolerant orchestration of
  long-running computational workflows. The platform integrates molecular
  structure tools with ORCA-based quantum-chemistry workflows and supports
  execution through user-owned Kaggle computational environments. Its
  orchestration architecture is designed to tolerate hosted-notebook session
  limits and web-service interruptions through explicit workflow state
  management, verified checkpoints, idempotent operations, execution leases,
  reconciliation, and watchdog-based recovery. The platform also provides
  tools for preparing computational inputs, managing calculation workflows,
  monitoring execution, and analyzing ORCA results in a reproducible
  research-oriented environment.
